[ti:Week04-Tues.mp3]

[00:00.00]peak 熟义 n. 顶峰；山峰；尖头‖v. 达到高峰‖a. 高峰时期的，巅峰状态的 示例 ① Should the trend continue, the number of tourists this year will finally top the 2000 peak. 如果这种趋势延续下去，今年游客的人数最终将比2000年的峰值还多。（2008. 6）② Traffic reaches its peak between 5 and 6 in the afternoon. 下午5点到6点之间交通达到高峰。
[00:07.43]riot 熟义 n. 暴乱，骚乱‖v. 发生骚乱，闹事 示例 ① There they found themselves competing for jobs and housing with immigrants from Europe. The competition was often violent, as in the Chicago riot of 1919, when 38 people were killed. 他们 （黑人）发现自己必须与欧洲来的移民竞争工作与住处，这种竞争经常是充满暴力的， 如1919年的芝加哥种族暴乱就有38人死亡。（Scientific American） ② Two prison guards were killed when a riot broke out in the jail. 两位狱警在监狱骚乱中遇难。
[00:18.36]minor 熟义 a. 较小的，次要的，轻微的‖n. 辅修科目 示例 ① Many doctors and researchers believe that loneliness harms the immune system, making us more vulnerable to a range of minor and major illnesses. 许多医生和研究者认为孤独损害免疫系统，使人们更容易受到一系列大大小小疾病的侵袭。（2010. 6）② He was lucky to escape with minor injuries. 他成功逃脱而只受了一点轻伤，真是万幸。
[00:26.92]centimetre 熟义 n. 厘米，公分 示例 ① Scientists estimate that GJ1214b is about 2.7 times Earth's diameter and weighs about seven times as much, giving the planet a density of about 2 grams per cubic centimetre. 科学家们估计，GJ1214b 的直径大约是地球的2.7倍，质量约是地球的 7倍，其密度约为2克每立方厘米。（Science） ② His last throw was only two centimetres short of the world record. 他的最后一掷距世界纪录只差两厘米。
[00:36.96]contribute 熟义 v. 捐献，捐赠（尤指款或物）；投稿， 撰稿 示例 ① Should such imbalances continue, pessimists say, they could contribute to slower growth. 悲观人士称，如果这样的逆差持续下去，将会导致经济增长速度更加缓慢。（2011. 12） ② Amity between the two nations will contribute to the development of this region. 这两个国家间的和睦友好有助于这一地区的发展。
[00:45.15]segment 熟义 n. 部分；瓣‖v. 分割，划分 示例 ① In its defence, Google points out that it displays only small segments of books that are in copyright—arguing that such displays are "fair use". 谷歌辩称：它仅仅展示受版权保护书籍的几个小节——这种展示是“正当使用”。（2011. 12） ② Market researchers usually segment the population on the basis of social class and income. 市场研究人员通常按照社会阶层和收入划分人口。
[00:54.92]proportion 熟义 n. 份额；比例；均衡；大小，形状 示例 ① The school had its first-ever black homecoming. Last spring the school graduated the same proportion of minorities as it did whites. 学校有了第一个黑人校友日。去年春季，该校少数民族毕业生比例与白人毕业生相当。（2011. 6）② Payment should be in proportion to the work done, not to the time spent. 工资应与完成的工作量成比例，而不是与花费的时间成比例。
[01:04.15]advocate 熟义 vt. 拥护，支持，提倡‖n. 拥护者，提倡者；辩护律师 示例 ① Advocates of the practice have taken issue with his team's use of such evidence as news accounts to support his conclusion that goal-setting is widely over-prescribed. （施维泽的）团队使用新闻报道作为证据，支持他的结论：目标设定已普遍滥用。对此，支持目标设定的人士持有异议。（2012. 6） ② The host will often need to play devil's advocate in order to get an interview going. 主持人常常需要故意唱反调以使得采访能够继续下去。
[01:15.42]confidential 熟义 a. 机密的；秘密的；受信任的 示例 ① A Manhattan judge ruled that the city may release performance rankings of thousands of teachers to the public, denying a request by the teachers union to keep the teachers' names confidential. 曼哈顿的一名法官裁决，该市（纽约市）可以将数以千计的教师表现排名公之于众，否决了教师协会对教师姓名保密的要求。（The New York Times）② Don't be too confidential with others. 不要过分地信任他人。
[01:25.76]induce 熟义 vt. 劝说，诱使；引起，导致 示例 ① The problem with reading in the car is that your vision is fixed on an object that is not moving, but your body and inner ear perceive motion, so it can induce vertigo. 在车里阅读会有一个问题： 你的视觉固定在一个不会移动的物体上，但你的身体和内耳却能够察觉到移动，而这样就会引起眩晕。（The New York Times）② Nothing in this world would induce me to take that job. 什么也不能诱使我接受那份工作。
[01:35.66]sensible 熟义 a. （人或行为）明智的，合理的；意识到的 示例 ① Crucially, as they (China and India) opened up their markets, they balanced market economy with sensible government direction. 至关重要的是，随着市场的开放，中国和印度在市场经济与明智的政府导向之间取得了平衡。（2012. 6） ② The seriously wounded guard was speechless but still sensible. 那个受了重伤的保镖不能说话了，但仍有知觉。
[01:44.59]radar 熟义 n. 雷达 示例 ① The National Weather Service hopes new radar upgrades will better predict severe weather this year—and save lives. 国家气象局希望今年新升级的雷达可以更好地预测恶劣天气，进而拯救生命。（Research） ② An unidentified flying object was detected by our radar. 一个不明飞行物被我方雷达发现了。
[01:51.98]advisable 熟义 a. 可取的，明智的 示例 ① It is always advisable for businesses to look beyond the price tag and look for a business-only provider that can offer more reliability, with good support. 因此企业最好不要只看价格，而要找专门为企业服务的、更可靠的、能够提供更好技术支持的供应商。（2009. 12） ② It is advisable to book tickets early. 早订票是明智的。
[02:00.31]bounce 熟义 v. （使）弹起，弹跳‖n. 弹跳；弹性； 活力 示例 ① Sounds bounce off heavy storm clouds and return to earth with increased force. 声音从厚厚的乌云反弹回来，以更加强大的力量回到地面。（2008. 12）② She has had a lot of difficulties, but she seems to bounce back pretty quickly. 她遇到过很多困难，但她似乎总能很快振作起来。
[02:07.70]region 熟义 n. 地区，区域；行政区 示例 ① Yet the growth of cities and industry is reducing the amount of water available for agriculture in many regions. 但是城市和工业的发展导致很多地区的农业用水资源越来越少。（2008. 12）② She is an authority in the region of linguistics. 她是语言学界的权威。
[02:14.56]rhythm 熟义 n. 节奏，韵律，律动 示例 ① It is evident that exercise will help to regulate our bodily clocks and circadian rhythms, especially as we enter middle age. 很明显，体育锻炼能帮助我们调整生物钟和生理节奏，尤其是当我们步入中年时。（The New York Times） ② The rhythm of this poem was destroyed by the poet's bad phrasing. 这首诗的韵律由于诗人措辞不当而被破坏了。
[02:23.05]decent 熟义 a. 像样的；（人或行为举止）合乎礼节的；得体的 示例 ① My camera has a set of handy, point-and-shoot settings that enable a bumbler like me to take decent pictures most of the time. 我的相机有一套简单的、 对准即拍设置，可以使我这种笨手笨脚的人在多数情况下拍出不错的照片。（New Scientist） ② There is a need for more resources so that all migrant workers may have a decent living condition. 我们需要更多的财力支持以使所有外来务工者都有良好的生活环境。
[02:33.36]trend 熟义 n. 趋势，倾向，动态 示例 ① So forecasting long range trends and making predictions on the basis of present evidence is what I do. 所以，预测长期的趋势并且以现实证据为基础做出一些预言是我的工作。（2013. 6）② Girls like to follow the latest trends in fashion. 女孩们喜欢追求最新的流行款式。
[02:40.14]precise 熟义 a. 准确的；恰好的；一丝不苟的 示例 ① Directionally, they capture the trends, but the idea that we know precisely how many are unemployed is a myth. 就方向而言，它们（这些数据）能够体现趋势，但如果说我们准确地知道失业人数，却是一句谎话。（2013. 6）② Probability is more often a disguise of our ignorance of the facts, than a precise description of the chance of happening. 可能性往往掩饰了我们对事实的无知，而不是对发生几率的准确描述。
[02:50.35]reveal 熟义 vt. 揭示，透露；显示 示例 ① Their work is already starting to reveal how the "Obama effect" is changing people's views and behaviour. 他们的工作已开始揭示出“奥巴马效应”是如何改变人们的观点和行为的。（2010. 6）② Systematic excavation of the ruins revealed a city roughly elliptical in shape. 系统地发掘这片废墟后发现了一座大体呈椭圆形的城市。
[02:58.57]homogeneous 熟义 a. 有相同特征的，同种类的 示例 ① One of the three problems with Britain's tech ecology is the absence of a market as big and homogeneous as American tech firms enjoy. 英国科技大环境存在的三个问题之一是，缺乏类似美国科技企业所享有的大型产业市场。（New Scientist）② Finland has a largely literate and relatively homogeneous population, little immigration and almost no poverty or social problems. 芬兰人口受教育比例高而且构成相对简单，几乎没有移民，也很少存在贫困和社会问题。
[03:10.11]portray 熟义 vt. 描绘；给人以某种印象 示例 ① Unlike conventional superheroes such as Superman, who stood for justice, fairness and decency, the modern macho superheroes portray a negative masculinity, characterize by mindless aggression and rampant sexism. 不同于传统超级英雄如超人所代表的正义、公正和正直的形象，现代强壮的超级英雄塑造出的却是负面的硬汉形象，他们愚昧好斗而且又有强烈的性别歧视。（The Guardian） ② The novel The Canterbury Talesportrays vividly the medieval English society and characters from all walks of life. 小说《坎特伯雷故事集》生动地描绘了中世纪的英国社会和各行各业的人物。
[03:24.30]peer 熟义 n. 身份（或地位）相同的人，同辈；（英国）贵族成员‖vi. 仔细看，端详 示例 ① John Rother, the AARP's head of policy and strategy, points to studies showing that other things being equal, people who remain at work have lower death rates than their retired peers. 美国退休人员协会政策与策略主管约翰•罗瑟引用一些研究成果证明，在同等条件下，一直工作的人要比退休的人的死亡率低。（2010. 12） ② I had been peering at a computer document. 我那会儿一直在细看一份电子文件。
[03:34.83]confuse 熟义 vt. 使迷惑；混淆；使更难于理解 示例 ① But as a recent study has shown, too many choices can make us confused, unhappy—even paralysed with indecision. 但是最近的研究显示，太多的选择机会会使我们感到困惑和不愉快——甚至失去做决断的能力。（2011. 6）② She always confuses between green and blue. 她总是分不清绿色和蓝色。
[03:42.26]arrange 熟义 v. 安排，筹备；布置 示例 ① I, personally arranged for the demonstration against radioactive waste dumping in the Atlantic Ocean. 我亲自安排示威游行，反对向大西洋中倾倒放射性废料。（2008. 12）② We are asked to arrange the desks and chairs in a circle when we make self-introduction in the first class. 第一堂课做自我介绍时，我们被要求把桌椅摆成一个圆圈。
[03:50.92]inner 熟义 a. 里面的；向内的；内心的 示例 ① And for those who like the idea of free-range kids but still struggle with their inner helicopter parent, there may be a middle way. 对于那些赞成自由放养孩子的想法但是仍然挣扎于内心的直升机式父母想法的父母而言，可能有一种折中的方式。（2009. 6）② The destructive spiral of violence finally boiled over in the inner-city riots. 日益严重的暴力行为最终演变成为市中心的暴乱。
[04:00.32]individual 熟义 a. 单独的，个别的；一个人的‖n. 个人 示例 ① The origins, though not the cause of Ebola Sudan, can be traced back to a single individual in a Sudanese town. 虽然这并非是苏丹型埃博拉病毒产生的原因，但是其来源可以追溯到苏丹某个城镇里的一例病例个案。（2013. 6）② The significance of garbage sorting must be made known to every household and individual. 垃圾分类的重要性要做到家喻户晓。
[04:09.38]forbid 熟义 vt. 禁止，不准；阻碍 示例 ① Most importantly, it would lift regulations that forbid local housing agencies from borrowing to cover building repairs, a common practice in the real estate industry. 最重要的是，这将解除当地房产机构不准借钱支付建筑修缮费用的禁令。借钱支付建筑修缮费用是房地产业通常的做法。（The New York Times） ② Some countries' constitution forbids the military use of nuclear energy. 一些国家的宪法禁止将核能用于军事用途。
[04:20.02]sin 熟义 n. 罪恶；罪行；过错‖v. 犯戒律，犯过失 示例 ① Sin is in on Wall Street as investors pick vice over virtue and pour money into drinking, smoking and gambling stocks. 罪恶正在华尔街上演着， 投资者选择了邪恶而摒弃了美德，他们花大笔金钱购买烟酒和博彩公司的股票。（USA Today） ② We must make atonement for our sins. 我们必须赎自己的罪过。
[04:27.51]stereo 熟义 n. 立体声音响（系统） 示例 ① The speakers of my old stereo finally gave out and there was no way to repair them. 我的旧音响的扬声器最终出毛病了，而且（这次）说什么也修不好了。（2011. 12）② She received a stereo radio from her father as her birthday gift. 她父亲送给她一台立体声收音机作为生日礼物。
[04:34.37]jury 熟义 n. 陪审团；（比赛的）裁判委员会 示例 ① The jury believed the testimony of the two victims, who positively identified Jackson as the man who had attacked them. 陪审团相信两名受害人的证词，这两名受害人断然认定杰克逊就是那个袭击她们的人。（2012. 6） ② Though the defendant's lawyer made compelling arguments, the jury were unconvinced that he was innocent. 尽管被告的律师做了令人信服的辩护，陪审团仍不相信他是无辜的。
[04:44.13]adequate 熟义 a. 足够的，合格的 示例 ① Recently, the UK National Stem Cell Network warned the UK could lose its place among the world leaders in stem cell research unless adequate funding and legislation could be assured. 最近，英国国家干细胞网络发出警告说：如果不能保证得到足够的资金和立法支持，英国将在干细胞研究方面失去世界领军地位。（2011. 12） ② This team is now counting the cost of its drought of adequate leadership. 这个团队现在尝到缺少合格领导人的苦头了。
[04:54.94]earnest 熟义 a. 非常认真的，诚实的，真诚的 示例 ① Despite decades of earnest researches, astronomers had no direct evidence that planets circle other stars. 尽管历经数十年的认真研究，天文学家仍然没有直接证据证明那些行星围绕其他恒星运转。（Scientific American） ② While you work, you should work in earnest. 当你工作时，你应投入其中。
[05:02.60]portion 熟义 n. 部分；一份；分享的部分‖v. 把…分成若干份 示例 ① But while much of the research and innovation has concentrated on finding less-polluting energy alternatives, it may be decades before clean technologies like wind and solar meet a significant portion of our energy needs. 然而，尽管大量研究和创新方法都专注于寻找污染相对较少的替代能源，但或许还要等上几十年，像风能和太阳能这类无污染技术才能够大量满足我们巨大的能源需求。（2012. 6） ② A major portion of the blame for this business crisis must be borne by the manager. 经理必须承担这次经营危机中的大部分责任。
[05:15.77]involve 熟义 vt. 包含；牵涉；使参加；表明 示例 ① This involves the study of sound structures, the formation of words, the sequencing of words and the construction of meaning, as well as examination of the theories explaining these aspects of English usage. 这包括对声音结构的研究、 对构词法的研究、对词序的研究、对意义建构的研究以及对解释这些方面英语用法的理论的检验。（2009. 6）② The corruption scandal revealed yesterday brings much notoriety to those officials involved in it. 昨天曝光的腐败丑闻使相关的官员声名狼藉。
[05:28.18]token 熟义 n. 代币；代金券；礼券‖a. 象征性的， 作为标志的 示例 ① The object, dated to around the first century AD, was protected from corrosion by the mud. Similar tokens have been found elsewhere in the Roman Empire, but this is the first time one has been unearthed in the UK. 这枚历史可以追溯至公元1世纪前后的硬币由于淤泥的保护而未受腐蚀。在罗马帝国的其他地方也曾出土过类似的硬币，但在英国尚属首次。（The Daily Telegraph） ② The local government has only made a token gesture towards helping the poor. 地方政府不过是做做样子表示一下对贫困人群的帮助。
[05:40.86]institute 熟义 n. (教育、专业等)机构，机构建筑‖v. 制定（体系、政策等），开始，实行 示例 ① When Stephen Covey, founder and director of the Leadership Institute, explored leadership styles in the past decade, he focused on the habits of a great number of highly effective individuals. 过去十年，领导力协会的创始人兼主管斯蒂芬•柯维在探索领导风格时，着重研究了大量高效能人士的习惯。（2011. 12） ② The police instituted an inquiry into the causes of the accident. 警方开始调查事故的原因。
[05:52.16]protein 熟义 n. 蛋白质 示例 ① A low-carbohydrate, high-protein diet may increase the risk for cardiovascular disease, according to a large study in Swedish women. 一项针对瑞典妇女所做的大型研究表明，低碳水化合物、高蛋白的饮食习惯可能会增加患心血管疾病的风险。（The New York Times）② Enough protein in the diet is essential to life. 饮食中足够的蛋白质是必不可少的。
[06:00.63]economic 熟义 a. 经济的；有利可图的 示例 ① "When you see things like Ford moving new production from Mexico to Detroit, instead of the other way around, you know things are changing," says Gene Sperling, director of the National Economic Council. 国家经济委员会主任吉恩•斯珀林说：“福特公司将新产品生产从墨西哥转移到底特律，而不是从底特律转移到墨西哥，当你看到类似的情况时，你就会明白，事情正在发生变化。”（2013. 6） ② We should blaze a new trail to industrialisation featuring high scientific and technological content, good economic returns, low resources consumption, little environmental pollution and a full display of advantages in human resources. 我们应该走出一条科技含量高、 经济效益好、资源消耗低、环境污染少、人力资源得到充分发挥的新型工业化路子。
[06:18.65]anxiety 熟义 n. 焦虑；害怕；渴望 示例 ① This should have primed the subjects with "stereotype threat"—an anxiety that their results will confirm negative stereotypes, which has been shown to damage the performance of African Americans. 这使得参与者中产生了一种叫做“成见威胁”的焦虑症状，即担心测试结果会证实对他们的负面成见，而这种焦虑经证实会影响非洲裔美国人的表现。（2010. 6） ② Rising tide of crime in that country gives some causes for anxiety. 那个国家日益增长的犯罪率令人担忧。
